## A. Recommended Architecture and Key State Machine

### A.1 Architecture Overview

```
+-----------+          Shared Memory (0x48c3c000, 128KB)         +-----------+
|           |  0x48c3c000 +--------+--------+ 0x48c4c000 +--------+           |
|  Linux    |----------->| vring0 | vring1 |            |  Pool  |<-----------|
|  A-core   |  MBOX7 A2B +--------+--------+            +--------+ B2A vqid0 |
|           |  (IRQ 116)  (0x8000) (0x8000)             (0x10000) MBOX4 B2A  |  HPMCU
|           |                                                     MBOX7 B2A  |  NuttX
+-----------+                                          vqid1       +-----------+
                                       Platform-only static
                                       resource table in HPMCU
                                       private RAM (not in SHM)
```

**Key architectural decisions:**
- **Platform-only resource table**: A static `struct rptun_rsc_s` in HPMCU BSS, allocated by the caller (not in shared memory at 0x48c3c000). Pattern follows `rptun_bmp.c` caller-owned table.
- **Identity address environment**: No `get_addrenv` op needed; DA = PA for HPMCU flat memory model.
- **V2.0 STATUS busy detection**: No LOCK/VERSION registers; use STATUS register read-check for TX busy.
- **Single RX IRQ**: MBOX7 A2B (IRQ 116 = HPMCU_MBOX3_BB_IRQn). Linux sends all notifications through this single channel.
- **Dual TX path**: vqid 0 -> MBOX4 B2A, vqid 1 -> MBOX7 B2A, matching confirmed transport contract.
- **DRIVER_OK pre-set**: Pre-set `VIRTIO_CONFIG_STATUS_DRIVER_OK` in static resource table; Linux `set_status` is a no-op anyway.

### A.2 State Machine

```
INIT:
  rv1126b_rptun_init("ap")
    -> memzero dev struct
    -> dev->master = false
    -> Initialize static resource table (pre-set all fields including DRIVER_OK)
    -> rv1126b_mailbox_init(callback, dev)  [configure RX, TX instances]
         -> Configure MBOX7 A2B_INTEN = TX_DONE | TRIG_MODE
         -> Configure MBOX4 B2A_INTEN = TRIG_MODE only
         -> Configure MBOX7 B2A_INTEN = TRIG_MODE only
         -> Clear all STATUS registers
         -> irq_attach(IRQ 116, isr, NULL)
         -> up_enable_irq(IRQ 116)
    -> rptun_initialize(&dev->rptun)
         -> Framework spawns rptun thread
              -> rptun_do_start
                   -> get_resource() returns static table (IMMEDIATE, no polling)
                   -> remoteproc_set_rsc_table
                   -> remoteproc_start
                   -> register_callback
              -> rptun_create_devices loop
                   -> Sees DRIVER_OK pre-set -> creates vdev
                   -> Registers rpmsg_virtio device

NORMAL OPERATION:
  Linux sends first handshake:
    Linux writes MBOX7 A2B CMD=0x03, DATA=0x524D5347
    -> MBOX7 A2B interrupt fires (IRQ 116)
    -> ISR: read CMD, read DATA, validate magic, W1C STATUS, barrier, call callback
    -> rptun_callback -> remoteproc_get_notification(RPTUN_NOTIFY_ALL)
    -> Processes vrings, rpmsg comes up

  HPMCU sends notification:
    rp_notify(dev, vqid)
    -> Check STATUS busy on target B2A (spin-wait up to ~100us)
    -> Write CMD=0x03, BARRIER, write DATA=0x524D5347
    -> Return (Linux ISR handles remainder)
```

